# Managing scenes in /poggy

The **Scenes** tab is the main admin tool for placed scenes. It lists every
scene on the server and changes them at once for every player: no restart, no
walking over to each one.

Open **/poggy** → **Poggy Scene** → **Scenes**.

## What you see

| Column | What it is |
|---|---|
| **ID** | The scene's number. |
| **Text** | The text as written, colour codes (`~e~`, `~t6~` …) included. |
| **Placed by** | The character's name and id. |
| **Where** | Its position (x, y, z). |
| **Placed** | When it was placed. Scenes from before version 1.3.2 show no date. |

Search and sort work as in any list, so searching a name finds everything that
player placed.

## Change a scene

- **Fix the text:** click it and edit. Everyone sees the new text straight away.
- **Delete:** the row's button, then confirm.
- **Delete all by this player:** removes every scene that character placed.
  You type the scene's id to confirm.

## Clean up old scenes

**Delete all older than…** at the top of the table:

1. Give a number of days, for example `30`.
2. Choose whether scenes with **no date** (placed before 1.3.2) go too.
3. Type `CONFIRM`.

Scenes never expire on their own, so this is how you keep the world tidy.

## Good to know

- Removing here is the same as a player pressing **4** by the scene: it
  disappears for everyone at once and is deleted from the database.
- Only people who may edit settings in `/poggy` can use this panel.
- Every change is printed to the server console with who made it, and shows in
  `/poggy`'s **History**.
